# Line endings are normalised to LF everywhere.
#
# Without this file, Git on Windows honours `core.autocrlf=true` and checks
# every text file out with CRLF, while the blobs stored in the repository are
# LF. Prettier defaults to `endOfLine: "lf"`, so `prettier --check` then failed
# on ~129 files on a Windows clone and passed in CI on Linux — a difference that
# has nothing to do with the code and cannot be fixed by formatting, because the
# next checkout puts the CRLFs straight back.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides `core.autocrlf` per-repository, so the working tree matches
# the blobs and the formatter agrees with itself on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts must keep CRLF or cmd.exe mis-parses them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary

# Lockfiles are generated. Collapsing them in diffs keeps reviews readable.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
poetry.lock linguist-generated=true -diff
